let __v_5893 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"{age} is not the problem — the trap is going for the same jobs as people half your age. Apply for the ones that ask for someone who has done it before.\",\"Age is a real filter in some places and invisible in others. What gets read is a CV that says what you ran, how big it was and what it saved, not a list of dates.\",\"The roles worth having at your age are the senior versions of what you were doing, and the quickest way in is the people who already know your work. Ask them before the job boards.\",\"You have years of doing the job properly, and that is what you are selling. Most people who land well at your age do it through somebody who has seen them work.\",\"It is a fair thing to worry about and it is survivable: apply upwards rather than sideways, and lead the CV with what you fixed and what it was worth.\",\"{age} is young for the jobs worth having. What were you doing before? I can tell you how to pitch it.\"]}")?;
