let __v_6179 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[\"known\",{\"$tuple\":[\"Since there is already a diagnosis, make this change the GP's problem rather than yours to watch: a step down like that is often something treatable, and an infection is the usual one they check for first.\",\"Ring the GP about your {who} rather than waiting for the next appointment — a change that comes on over days rather than months is often something with a fix, and worth saying today.\"]}],[\"homeward\",{\"$tuple\":[\"That's a relief — home is where most of the getting better happens. How is your {who} in themselves?\",\"Good news. Keep the first week small: short visits, early nights, and let your {who} set the pace rather than the other way round.\",\"Home, then — that is the bit that matters. The first days back are the ones to keep quiet, because everyone tries to do too much in them.\",\"Glad to hear it, and home beats a ward for getting better. Ask what to watch for in your {who}'s first fortnight, and who to ring if something changes.\"]}],[\"diagnosed\",{\"$tuple\":[\"I'm sorry - a diagnosis like that changes the shape of a week. How is your {who} in themselves?\",\"Worrying news. What have they said about what happens next, and who is looking after your {who}'s care?\",\"That is a lot to take in, and it takes time to sink in. Has anyone walked you through the treatment yet?\"]}],[\"hospital\",{\"$tuple\":[\"Sorry to hear that. How is your {who} doing?\",\"That is a worrying place for your {who} to be. What has the hospital said?\",\"Worrying, and waiting is the worst part of it. How is your {who} in themselves?\"]}],[\"memory\",{\"$tuple\":[\"Losing track of things in a familiar place is worth a word with your {who}'s GP, and soon: it can be a lot of things and several of them are fixable. A note of when it started, and anything else that has changed, is what they ask for first.\",\"That is worth mentioning to a GP rather than waiting to see if it settles. Write down what you have noticed about your {who} and when it started, and take that with you — and if it gets suddenly worse, that is the same day rather than next week.\",\"Worth a GP appointment with your {who}, and take this line with you: forgetting things in a place they know well is the kind of change that gets looked at properly, and the sooner the easier it usually is.\"]}],[\"falls\",{\"$tuple\":[\"A fall is worth getting looked at even when nothing hurts, and a second one is worth a GP visit: balance, eyesight and medicines are the usual causes and all three can be helped. Clear the loose rugs and put a lamp within reach of the bed in the meantime.\",\"Falls are rarely just age, and that is the good news: strength, eyesight and medication are the places to look, and a GP can start on all three. Until then, good light on the stairs and nothing to trip over on the way to the bathroom.\"]}],[\"care\",{\"$tuple\":[\"Ask the staff what they notice day to day and get it written in the home's notes — they see more of your {who} than you can, and a GP takes their record seriously. Visit at different times of day so you see it for yourself too.\",\"A home keeps a daily record, so ask what is in it about your {who}: eating, sleep, and anything that has changed. That is the account a GP or the manager can act on, and it costs you one conversation at the desk.\"]}],[\"sleep\",{\"$tuple\":[\"Broken sleep is worth reading rather than enduring: pain, a new tablet, drinking later, a room that is too warm, worry — one of those is usually behind it, and the fix is different for each. If it has been weeks, or they are worn out all day, ring the GP: a blood test rules out the physical ones.\",\"A night that is nothing like their usual is a change worth having looked at, and sooner if it came on suddenly. Ring the GP this week and say when it started and what is different about the nights now.\"]}],[\"low\",{\"$tuple\":[\"Going quiet and off things is worth saying out loud to a GP — it is common, it is treatable, and people often do not mention it themselves. One small thing a week that gets your {who} out, even a short walk, does more than a big plan.\",\"That kind of withdrawal is worth a GP appointment rather than a wait: low mood in later life is under-reported and it responds to help. In the meantime, keep the visits going even when they say no — company is the bit that works.\"]}],[\"ill\",{\"$tuple\":[\"Get your {who} looked at rather than waiting it out, and sooner if it is getting worse — a change like that in someone you are looking after is worth a proper check.\",\"Worth a GP appointment for your {who} this week rather than next month, and keep a note of what has changed and when. If it turns sudden, that is the same day.\"]}]]}")?;
