let __v_7978 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Pick the moment rather than the words: not mid-argument and not as they walk out. Ask for two minutes, say the one sentence, and let them answer it.\",\"Say it once and then let them talk. The explaining is what turns a repair back into the row.\",\"Don't ask them to tell you it's fine. Say what you got wrong, then let them be annoyed or not - that part is theirs.\",\"Ask what they heard. If it is not what you meant, that is the next sentence, and it is worth saying rather than arguing.\",\"Let what you do next carry it: the few days after matter more than the apology itself.\"]}")?;
frame.store("SAID_WRONG_NEXT", __v_7978.clone())?;
let __v_7979 = { let __v_7980 = frame.load(rt, "repair")?; rt.getattr(&__v_7980, "ASKS_FOR_THE_WORDS")? };
frame.store("ASKS_FOR_THE_WORDS", __v_7979.clone())?;
let __v_7981 = { let __v_7982 = frame.load(rt, "repair")?; rt.getattr(&__v_7982, "ASKS_WHAT_TO_DO")? };
frame.store("ASKS_WHAT_TO_DO", __v_7981.clone())?;
let __v_7983 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Say it sooner than feels comfortable, and name the sentence itself rather than hinting at it: people forgive a plain \\\"that came out badly, I didn't mean it\\\" far more easily than a vague apology for everything.\",\"Keep it to what you said and that you got it wrong. The explaining is the part that makes it land as an excuse, so leave it for later, or out.\",\"Own the one sentence, not everything around it: naming the exact thing you regret shows you heard it, and a general apology mostly sounds like you want it over with.\",\"Most people want to know you noticed, not that you are sorry in general, so go back and say which bit was wrong. It costs you a minute and it is usually the whole repair.\",\"It is fixable, and the fix is a sentence rather than a gesture. Say the one thing you got wrong, plainly, and stop there - they can be annoyed while you leave the details alone.\"]}")?;
frame.store("SAID_WRONG_REPLIES", __v_7983.clone())?;
let __v_7984 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Own it before they have to bring it up, and keep it to one sentence: what you did, that you are sorry, and what you will do instead. The explaining can come later, or not at all.\",\"Say the plain version first - name what you did, say you are sorry, and add no reason unless they ask for one - then do the small thing you can actually do this week.\",\"The apology is the small part; the change is the rest. Name what you did once, then let the next few weeks show it rather than repeating it every time you speak.\",\"Put it right sooner than feels comfortable, and name the one thing rather than a list of everything you feel bad about. People forgive a specific \\\"I got that wrong\\\" far more easily than a general apology for a whole week.\",\"Say what you did, then stop. Adding why is the part that sounds like an excuse, and they can be annoyed for a bit without you talking them out of it.\"]}")?;
frame.store("DEED_REPLIES", __v_7984.clone())?;
let __v_7985 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Do it today, before you explain anything: the call, the visit, the present that is late arriving. Then say the one line - \\\"I left it too long and I'm sorry\\\" - because a reason offered first sounds like the reason you did not.\",\"Ring rather than message, and lead with them rather than with your week: they have been waiting, and what they want to hear is that you know it. Put the next one in your phone before you hang up.\",\"Name the gap once, plainly, and then be there: \\\"It's been too long and that's on me.\\\" A visit or a call booked this week says the rest, and asking them to reassure you costs them the thing you owe them.\",\"Pick the smallest real thing that ends the gap today - a call on the walk home, a note, a date in the diary with the day fixed - and do that rather than plan a bigger gesture later.\"]}")?;
frame.store("LEFT_IT_TOO_LONG_REPLIES", __v_7985.clone())?;
let __v_7986 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Own it today, and take the sting out of it by naming the day: \\\"I got the date wrong and I'm sorry - it isn't that it doesn't matter.\\\" Then book the thing, because a make-up that happens this week beats a bigger sorry that stays a plan.\",\"Say it before they have to ask, and don't hide behind the date: \\\"I knew it was coming and I still let it pass, and I'm sorry.\\\" Then do the specific thing - a dinner, a card, a visit - rather than waiting to be forgiven.\",\"Ring rather than text, and keep it to the one thing: you missed the day, you are sorry, and here is what you are doing about it. A late card that arrives is worth more than an apology that asks them to tell you it is fine.\"]}")?;
frame.store("FORGOT_DATE_REPLIES", __v_7986.clone())?;
let __v_7987 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Name it in one line and stop: \\\"I let you down over this and I'm sorry - that was my doing.\\\" Then the one thing you are doing about it, because a sentence with a next step in it is heard as meant rather than as sorry-sounding.\",\"Say what you did, that it was yours, and leave why out of the first sentence: \\\"I got that wrong and I'm sorry.\\\" If they ask why, answer it then; before that it arrives as a defence.\",\"Start with the thing they are owed rather than how bad you feel: \\\"You had every right to be annoyed with me, and I'm sorry.\\\" Then ask what would help, and do that one thing.\",\"Keep it short and specific: what you did, that you are sorry, and the change they can see in the next few weeks. \\\"I'm sorry - I won't do that again\\\" is worth more when you name which \\\"that\\\" was.\"]}")?;
frame.store("DEED_WORDS", __v_7987.clone())?;
let __v_7988 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"\\\"I missed your birthday and I'm sorry - I'm not going to pretend I was saving it up.\\\" Say that on the phone rather than in a message, then ask when they are free this week, so the next thing after the apology is a date in the diary.\",\"\\\"I got the day wrong and I've felt rotten about it all week.\\\" Naming the day is what makes it land as an oversight rather than as not caring, and it is the one thing they are waiting to hear.\",\"Lead with the sorry and then the plan: \\\"I'm sorry I let it go by - I've booked a table for Friday, if you're free.\\\" The booking is the apology; asking them to reassure you is not.\"]}")?;
frame.store("FORGOT_DATE_WORDS", __v_7988.clone())?;
let __v_7989 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Pick the one thing they would actually notice and do it this week: the visit, the lift they always ask for, the money paid back, the afternoon spent with the child. Amends is a verb - what they are owed is the thing made good, not a longer apology.\",\"Say sorry for your part of it in one sentence, then ask them: \\\"what would help?\\\" once, and do that rather than what you would have chosen. Most people want the thing put right, and the ones who want to say their piece get to say it.\",\"Do it in their language rather than yours: if they tidy and cook, turn up and help with that rather than buying something. Then keep it up for a few weeks, because the change after the apology is the part that reads as meant.\",\"Start with the smallest real thing you can finish today - the call you have put off, the message that says you know you owe them - then tell them what you are doing about the rest rather than asking them to trust the intention.\"]}")?;
frame.store("AMENDS_REPLIES", __v_7989.clone())?;
let __v_7990 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Ring them today rather than waiting for a better moment, and keep it to the three things: you missed the day, you are sorry, and here is what you are doing about it. Then put the next one in your phone with a week's warning on it, because the second miss is the one that hurts.\",\"A card and a date beat a longer apology: book something they would like for this week and tell them the day rather than asking them to choose it. What they are owed now is the thing made up, not the explaining.\",\"Get the next one right in public: say the sorry once, then let the dinner or the visit do the rest. Bringing it up again a month later makes them do the forgiving twice.\"]}")?;
frame.store("FORGOT_DATE_NEXT", __v_7990.clone())?;
